course: dictionary
lesson: 15092
title: Rosary and prayer beads
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words name a thing you can hold, and the sentence tells you what it is for. «Mrs Costa took her rosary from her pocket and moved one bead at a time as she prayed.» A bead is a small ball with a hole through it, so a rosary must be made of beads, and moving them while praying tells you what it is used for.
explain: Clues often come from the words near the hard word. «In church, the children learned how Catholics say the rosary, one prayer for each bead.» Church and prayer are clues: the rosary belongs to religion, and saying it means saying a set of prayers. Ask yourself what would fit here. A string of beads for counting prayers fits.
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. Rosary can mean the beads, or the set of prayers said with them. It can also mean a rose garden, but that meaning is rare and old. In a sentence about praying, a rosary is the beads or the prayers, not a garden.
fact: A rosary is a string of beads used by Catholic Christians to count prayers.
fact: Saying the rosary means saying a set of prayers, including the Hail Mary and the Lord's Prayer.
fact: As each prayer is said, the person moves on to the next bead.
fact: Other faiths use prayer beads too, such as Muslims and Buddhists.
fact: Rosary is a noun, and its plural is rosaries.
exercise: «Mrs Costa held her rosary and moved one bead for each prayer.» What is a rosary? | A type of flower in a garden | A kind of warm coat | A hymn book | *A string of beads used to count prayers
exercise: «The Catholic family said the rosary together after dinner.» What does said the rosary mean here? | Sang a song in the kitchen | Read a story to the children | *Prayed a set of prayers, using beads to count them | Ate a special dessert
exercise: Which other faith, besides Catholics, uses prayer beads? | Bakers | *Buddhists | Pirates | Football fans
test: «The rosary lay on the table next to the old Bible.» What was the rosary most likely used for? | *Counting prayers with beads | Keeping warm | Sailing a boat | Watering the flowers
test: In an old book, «the rosary was full of red roses» means: | A string of prayer beads | A winter coat | A church bell | *A rose garden
exam: What is a rosary? | A type of bird | A kind of bread | *A string of beads used by Catholic Christians to count prayers | A church bell
